/-!
# The Sudoku proof's spread for interleaving

`fs4_interleave` asks of each proof its bound, its read list and the spread
`hsp` of every programmed coordinate.  For the Sudoku proof the first two
are `sud_fs4T` and `sudFS4T_hrd` (`sudFS4T_hrdD`); here the third: each
coordinate of a simulated point determines its first commitment, directly,
as its low digit mod `n1`, or through the read-back `dg` of the query hash
(`digitOf`, `coord_digit`), so the commitment's spread bounds every
coordinate's (`sudFS4T_hsp`, by `spread_sum`).  Together: `n` Sudoku proofs,
their openings reading at transcript points (`sudD`), interleaved with query
phases by any pattern (`sud_interleave`), the proofs' errors and the
collision term the only error, the hits charged at the first commitment's
spread `δs`.  With openings reading their data and salt as well (`sudDD`,
`pfRd`, by `sudFS4T_hrdD`): `sud_interleaveD`.  The hidden-term and composed
circuits likewise, their openings reading at transcript points
(`witFS4T_houtL`, `witFS4T_hrd`, `witFS4T_hsp`, `witD`, `wit_interleave`,
and the `comp` ones); with data-reading openings, `witFS4T_houtD`,
`witFS4T_hrdD`, `witDD`, `wit_interleaveD`, and the `comp` ones; with
openings reading at any digit, `sudDA`, `sud_interleaveA`. With a query
phase before each proof chosen from every earlier view and answer:
`sud_powQ` (`FSMultiPost`'s `fs4_powQ`; `sudD`'s openings, the `A`/`D`
variants and `wit`/`comp` not instanced).  Not shown: that FRI's challenges
are such openings (its commit phase is not modelled).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
namespace Circuit
open ZKF

/-- The first commitment a programmed coordinate's value `v` in table `tab`
    forces. -/
def digitOf (n1 : Nat) (dg : Nat → Nat) (tab v : Nat) : Nat :=
  match tab with
  | 0 => v
  | 1 => v % n1
  | 2 => v % n1
  | _ => dg v

theorem coord_digit {n1 : Nat} (dg : Nat → Nat) (p : Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat) (_h0 : p.1 < n1)
    (h1 : p.2.1 % n1 = p.1) (h2 : p.2.2.1 % n1 = p.1) (h3 : dg p.2.2.2 = p.1) (tab v : Nat)
    (e : coord4 tab p = v) : p.1 = digitOf n1 dg tab v := by
  match tab, e with
  | 0, e => exact e
  | 1, e => change p.2.1 = v at e; show p.1 = v % n1; rw [← e, h1]
  | 2, e => change p.2.2.1 = v at e; show p.1 = v % n1; rw [← e, h2]
  | j + 3, e => change p.2.2.2 = v at e; show p.1 = dg v; rw [← e, h3]

